---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, BUSINESS_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../utils/env';

const effectiveDateISO = '2026-08-29';
const effectiveDateLabel = 'August 29, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles data.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
  </header>

  <p>{APP_NAME} is published by {BUSINESS_NAME}.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} sends <SiteLink href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy/" target="_blank" aria-label="TelemetryDeck privacy policy, opens in new tab">TelemetryDeck</SiteLink> app use, purchases, crashes, how well the
      app runs, and app, device, and settings details, including accessibility
      settings, color scheme, language, layout direction, and region. It also
      sends a scrambled random ID, one per install, that lasts until the app's
      data is reset or the app is deleted. We use all of it to improve the app.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics can be turned off in the app's settings. That stops new data but
      does not delete what was sent. We set no deletion date, and the records
      hold no name or email, so one person's records cannot be found and
      deleted.
    </p>
    <p>
      TelemetryDeck has to protect this data at least as well as this policy and
      Apple's rules require.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Content reports</h2>
    <p>
      A content report is an email carrying the reason, round ID, app version,
      and build number, plus the reporter's email address and, only if they
      attach it, the drawing. We use it to look into the report.
    </p>
    <p>
      Report emails stay in our support inbox. To have one deleted, email <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink> from the address it was sent from.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Tracking</h2>
    <p>
      No one uses {APP_NAME} to track activity on other websites or in other
      companies' apps.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We post important changes to this policy here.</p>
  </section>

  <footer class="doc__meta">Effective <time datetime={effectiveDateISO}>{effectiveDateLabel}</time>.</footer>
</Doc>
